  "prefLabel": "He-W 637.17 High School Diploma or Equivalent",
  "priorExpiration": "2007-04-11",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-W 637.17 High School Diploma or Equivalent. Dependent children ages 16 and 17 who do not have a high school diploma or equivalent and who are mandatory NHEP participants shall participate full-time in an educational program that leads to a high school diploma or equivalency, as defined by the institution that provides the activity, to satisfy participation requirements pursuant to He-W 637.03.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at Chapter Heading He-W 600) #6446, eff 2-1-97; amd by #7206, eff 3-1-00; ss by #8269, eff 2-1-05; ss by #8740, INTERIM, eff 10-13-06, EXPIRED: 4-11-07\n\nNew. #8869, eff 4-19-07; ss by 10163, eff 7-26-12; ss by #13549, eff 2-1-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-w600.html"
